I want an easy tool for quick plotting in the terminal window, focusing on .xvg files produced with gromacs
Some examples are given in the directory

the comments usually follow the # whereas @ give some instructions about axis, titles etc following the xmgrace lingo

it is not essential to implement all this - i essenially want to be able to quickly produce a plot in the terminal window
with axis legends, mostly focusing on simple XY plots when two columns are given in the input file. when more than 2 columns are given
the user should be able to select which column should be the X and which column the Y axis. I also want to be able to plot two files of the same type at the same time, with automatically different symbols chosen, so I can easily compare two (or more) files from different simulations, conditions, etc

I am not sure what language is best to achieve this, so suggest some.



